From: Jon Pretty <jon.pretty@propensive.com>
Date: Fri, 17 Jul 2026 15:22:50 +0200
Subject: Widen bottom-typed call receivers to Object in the backend

A method call can reach genCallMethod with a receiver class of Null (or
Nothing), e.g. a member call on a value flow-typed to Null under
explicit nulls combined with capture checking. Bottom classes have no
runtime class ('Cannot create ClassBType for special class symbol
Null'), and the only members dispatchable on them are Object's, so the
invocation descriptor's receiver is widened to Object.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Proscala-Patch: nullreceiver
---
 .../src/dotty/tools/backend/jvm/BCodeBodyBuilder.scala | 10 ++++++++--
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/compiler/src/dotty/tools/backend/jvm/BCodeBodyBuilder.scala b/compiler/src/dotty/tools/backend/jvm/BCodeBodyBuilder.scala
index b814ab82ef4367908817e0a82ea3af91df263ffe..4f88f7699ede87b85da4a5d2045da8c4f6dae34d 100644
--- a/compiler/src/dotty/tools/backend/jvm/BCodeBodyBuilder.scala
+++ b/compiler/src/dotty/tools/backend/jvm/BCodeBodyBuilder.scala
@@ -1472,13 +1472,19 @@ trait BCodeBodyBuilder(val primitives: ScalaPrimitives) extends BCodeSkelBuilder
       }
 
       receiverClass.info // ensure types the type is up to date; erasure may add lateINTERFACE to traits
-      val receiverName = bTypeLoader.classBTypeFromSymbol(receiverClass).internalName
+      // A call can reach the backend with a bottom-typed receiver (e.g. a member call on a
+      // value flow-typed to `Null` under explicit nulls with capture checking); `Nothing`
+      // and `Null` have no runtime class, and the only members dispatchable on them are
+      // Object's, so widen the descriptor's receiver to Object.
+      val receiverClass1 =
+        if defn.isBottomClassAfterErasure(receiverClass) then defn.ObjectClass else receiverClass
+      val receiverName = bTypeLoader.classBTypeFromSymbol(receiverClass1).internalName
 
       val jname    = method.javaSimpleName
       val bmType   = bTypeLoader.methodBTypeFromSymbol(method)
       val mdescr   = bmType.descriptor
 
-      val isInterface = isEmittedInterface(receiverClass)
+      val isInterface = isEmittedInterface(receiverClass1)
       import InvokeStyle.*
       if (style == Super) {
         val ownerBType = bTypeLoader.bTypeFromType(method.owner.info)
